# Decided
- trueqbit: split out binary_operator, so assign_t can leave operators.h
  while it stays a binary_operator. Claude had leaned to keeping assign_t
  in operators.h, since a header of its own would still include
  operators.h for binary_operator.
- ast/binary_operator.h: binary_operator and is_binary_operator_v. Purpose
  "give the binary operator nodes their shared shape"; a helper of the
  node headers like operand_tags.h, its own Intention, not gathered by
  node_definitions.h (operators.h and assignment.h include it).
- ast/assignment.h: assign_string, assign_t, is_assign_v, assign().
  Purpose "represent the assignment of a SET clause"
  (https://www.sqlite.org/lang_update.html, "the list of assignments
  following the SET keyword"; the same SET serves an upsert's DO UPDATE).
  The shared node Intention; gathered by node_definitions.h after
  app_function.h. "assignment" is SQLite's word; in C++ it reads as
  operator=, which c(...) = ... is.
- quoted_expression.h includes assignment.h in place of operators.h: assign_t
  was all it used from there; operators.h still arrives through
  binary_condition.h.
- Moved comment reworded where it lands (ledger entry 16): "//  note: see
  `is_conc_v`" -> "//  note: see `is_conc_v` of `operators.h`".

